<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32978" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ōrĭcos</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ōrĭcus</span></b> , i,
			f., or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ōrĭcum</span></b> , i,
		n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὠρικός</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὠρικόν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a seaport town of Illyria
			Grœca</i>, now <i>Ericho</i>, <i><span class="en">Caes. B. C.
				3, 8 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 24, 40</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 3,
				12</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Prop. 1, 8, 20</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Luc. 3,
			187</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ōrĭcīni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Oricum</i>, <i>the
			Oricians</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Oricinorum fines,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					26, 25</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ōrĭcĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Oricum</i>, <i>Orician</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Oricia terebinthus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 10, 136</span></i>
			.</div>
